\begin{abstract}
We present VST-SIM V2.4, a high-performance, multi-GPU numerical relativity engine
implementing a vulcanized spacetime formulation of the Einstein field equations.
The system integrates: (i) a modified $3+1$ ADM decomposition with a non-linear
elastic hysteresis tensor $H_{\mu\alpha\beta}$, (ii) homomorphic CKKS encryption
for privacy-preserving astrophysical data ingestion and metric evolution, and
(iii) autonomous adaptive mesh refinement (AMR) and gauge control loops for
extreme curvature regimes. We report fourth-order convergence of ADM constraints,
high signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) under deep homomorphic evaluation, and robust
stability under extreme stress tests including near-singular energy densities,
lapse collapse, and high-Mach curvature shocks.
\end{abstract}

