\section{Numerical Methods and GPU Implementation}

\subsection{Time integration and dissipation}

We employ a fourth-order Runge--Kutta (RK4) or iterated Crank--Nicolson scheme
with Courant--Friedrichs--Lewy (CFL) factor
\begin{equation}
    C_{\text{CFL}} = 0.25, \qquad \Delta t = 0.005\,M
\end{equation}
for baseline runs, where $M$ is a characteristic mass scale.

Spatial dissipation is provided by a sixth-order Kreiss--Oliger operator with
coefficient
\begin{equation}
    \epsilon_{\text{KO}} = 0.02,
\end{equation}
which damps high-frequency numerical noise while preserving convergence order.

\subsection{Adaptive mesh refinement (AMR)}

We implement an octree-based AMR hierarchy with levels $L = 0,\dots,8$:
\begin{align}
    L = 0 &:~ \Delta x_0 = 0.08\,M, \\
    L = 4 &:~ \Delta x_4 = 0.005\,M, \\
    L = 8 &:~ \Delta x_8 \approx 3.125\times 10^{-4}\,M.
\end{align}
Local timesteps are constrained by the CFL condition,
\begin{equation}
    \Delta t \le C_{\text{CFL}} \frac{\Delta x_{\min}}{v_{\max}},
\end{equation}
where $v_{\max}$ is the maximum characteristic speed. Under extreme refinement,
$\Delta t$ is dynamically reduced (e.g., from $0.005\,M$ to $\sim 2\times10^{-5}\,M$)
to maintain stability.

\subsection{Tensor-level shock capturing kernel}

To handle sharp metric gradients, we employ a total variation diminishing (TVD)
shock capturing scheme coupled to a GPU kernel:

\begin{verbatim}
__global__ void EvaluateTensorShockKernel(
    const double* __restrict__ gamma_ij,
    const double* __restrict__ d_gamma_dx,
    double* __restrict__ hysteresis_flux,
    double shock_threshold,
    double eta_0,
    size_t grid_elements)
{
    size_t idx = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;
    if (idx >= grid_elements) return;

    double grad_norm = d_gamma_dx[idx];
    double adaptive_eta = eta_0 * fmin(1.0, grad_norm / shock_threshold);
    hysteresis_flux[idx] = adaptive_eta * grad_norm;
}
\end{verbatim}

The adaptive viscosity
\begin{equation}
    \eta_{\text{adaptive}} = \eta_0 \min\left(1,
        \frac{\norm{\nabla \gamma}}{\text{shock\_threshold}}
    \right)
\end{equation}
ensures bounded, monotone dissipation.

